Package: FastPCA
Title: Fast SVD, Randomized and Exact, with Missing-Value PCA
Version: 0.10.0
Authors@R:
    person("Alex", "Soupir", , "Alex.Soupir@moffitt.org",
           role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Fast randomized and exact singular value decomposition (SVD)
    for large matrices, aimed at the iterative workflows common in
    high-dimensional biological data analysis. Several computational backends
    are available: base R and 'irlba' require no Python, while optional
    PyTorch or tinygrad backends are accessed through the 'reticulate'
    package. Principal component analysis that tolerates missing values is
    provided by NIPALS(), with a reference implementation from the 'nipals'
    package. Principal component analysis of data that does not fit in memory is
    provided by IncrementalPCA(), which streams a list of chunk files (base R,
    PyTorch or tinygrad backends). Helpers for matrix transformation and UMAP
    embedding are also provided.
URL: https://github.com/ACSoupir/FastPCA, https://acsoupir.github.io/FastPCA/
BugReports: https://github.com/ACSoupir/FastPCA/issues
